# Cloudflare Pages security headers.
#
# Production deploys via .github/workflows/deploy.yml to Cloudflare Pages, so
# the "headers" block in firebase.json is never served — that file only applies
# to Firebase Hosting. Vite copies public/ to the root of dist/, which is where
# Pages looks for this file.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy yet: the pages rely heavily on inline scripts and
# CDN-hosted Tailwind and Firebase, so a policy needs to be worked out and
# tested page by page before it can be enforced.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
